  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foster a Culture of Peace, Non-Discrimination and Human Rights in Caribbean SIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caribbean Small Island Developing States are recognized as a priority group for UNESCO. In close coordination with a multi-stakeholder coalition, UNESCO will strengthen capacities of Member States and Associate Members to promote a culture of peace and advance effective policies and practices on human rights, intercultural understanding and ending all forms of discrimination and racism.

Leveraging a multifaceted approach UNESCO will produce knowledge and enhance skills, promote human rights and gender equality, combat discrimination, and promote intercultural dialogue and peacebuilding to foster inclusive societies. UNESCO will build on the ongoing Decade for People of African Descent (2015-2024), the UNESCO Roadmap Against Racism and Discrimination, as well as on the shared history on the Transatlantic Slave Trade and its consequences in the Caribbean sub-region.</narrative>
  </description>
